<activity xml:id="act-CycloidSlopes">
    <title>Slopes on a Cycloid</title>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            Consider the cycloid formed by a circle with radius <m>r=1</m>:
            <md>
                <mrow>x \amp = t-\sin(t)</mrow>
                <mrow>y \amp = 1-\cos(t)</mrow>
            </md>
            <figure xml:id="fig-cycloid">
                <caption>The cycloid.</caption>
                <image source="./ParametricPolar/cycloid.png" width="80%">
                    <shortdescription>The cycloid, visualized on the interval from 0 to approximately 4 pi. This looks like 2 arches, with bottoms at 0, 2 pi and 4 pi.</shortdescription>
                </image>
            </figure>
        </p>
    </introduction>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                First, make a conjecture: where do you think the cycloid will have horizontal tangent lines? What about vertical tangent lines, or other points where the derivative doesn't exist?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Find <m>\frac{dy}{dt}</m> and <m>\frac{dx}{dt}</m>, and construct <m>\dydx</m>.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Find the values of <m>t</m> where <m>\dydx = 0</m>.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Find the values of <m>t</m> where <m>\dydx</m> does not exist.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Use these values of <m>t</m> to find the points on the cycloid where there are horizontal tangent lines or points where the derivative doesn't exist. Do they match what you conjectured?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
</activity>